      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T02:16:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is going to result in a rule with an arbitrary number of output files, which will then all be used as inputs to another rule.  That seems like an unnecessary load on the build.ninja file an ninja.  I can think of a few ways to avoid that:\n\n - Always produce a zip file, and then the next rule can use zipsync to unzip them into a directory.\n - Return a partially filled out RuleBuilder that has the copy commands and let the caller add the packaging commands.\n - Support the various output formats directly in PackageModule.\n - Use single output file as the dependency, since they will always be created together.  This can cause problems if an untracked output file was manually deleted though.",
      "revId": "1b6b47f61c4abbdb8df8bcce1d3a1201a84307e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
